#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101624} :activity/id #uuid "cc587435-7439-5c7f-8921-a252025a9c6c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050100 :topic/id #uuid "2d1d35b9-13b1-5815-b3ec-f38b609cdc4c" :topic/math-academy-id 1213} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101624 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186102010 :tutorial/content "Let's remind ourselves of the general strategy for optimization problems:\n\n1\\. Draw a diagram of the situation, introducing variables where necessary.\n\n2\\. Write down the equation of the quantity that you're trying to maximize or minimize. This is called the **objective function**, and it might include more than one variable.\n\n3\\. Write down the constraint equation.\n\n4\\. Use the constraint equation to write the objective function in terms of a single variable only.\n\n5\\. Differentiate the objective function, set it equal to zero, and solve for the stationary points.\n\n6\\. Test each stationary point using the second derivative test. Or you can use the first derivative test if it's easier.\n\nWe can use differentiation to solve optimization problems involving boxes and trays, such as maximizing a box's volume given a fixed amount of material." :tutorial/id #uuid "7ae4bf43-6be2-587b-84fd-44fd4caa0064" :tutorial/math-academy-id 668 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "315afe75-f7a4-5846-97df-72ec811c4ef1" :step/math-academy-id 1281 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101625}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101625 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100838 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100648 :question/id #uuid "67870fdb-1d06-55a2-9955-e45d75e086cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-349"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30aa0a50-65a9-50fc-b7b2-8af1b327b708" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048883} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049878} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050020} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050622}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101221} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101364} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508916} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508934} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508943} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508970} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508974}] :knowledge-point/title "Maximizing the Volume of a Box With a Fixed Surface Area"} :step/id #uuid "1f4e36ee-7296-54c8-a529-9932e81ea024" :step/math-academy-id 1282 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101626}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101626 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100839 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100649 :question/id #uuid "e0481513-6849-54de-987e-7c0890002c68" :question/math-academy-id "e-350"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d32e1508-2254-5c4c-b220-98eadb13a57e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049179}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101220} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101275} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508925} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508937} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508952} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508958} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508988} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559798} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559851}] :knowledge-point/title "Minimizing the Surface Area of a Box With a Fixed Volume"} :step/id #uuid "560b0125-eaf6-5fba-ad27-32f240c547ef" :step/math-academy-id 1287 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101783}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101782 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100939 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100770 :question/id #uuid "db25170a-7b5f-5bbf-9ef9-31fd58d1b1e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-7146"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "980f8042-c7e5-510b-a818-f4c20fb96117" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050465}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101276} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101381} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508919} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508922} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508960} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508981} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508998} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559793}] :knowledge-point/title "Maximizing the Volume of a Tray"} :step/id #uuid "dceb3901-717c-5f81-9670-f473386eaea0" :step/math-academy-id 26330} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101783 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100940 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100771 :question/id #uuid "092110eb-85a7-5694-ad90-6797a4aff94d" :question/math-academy-id "e-7147"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ce295cc-ebc4-5dd0-83ec-d6d1741a237b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101222} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101542} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508915} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508935} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508978} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508985} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559826} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559827}] :knowledge-point/title "Optimizing the Cost of Building a Box"} :step/id #uuid "97f46a57-454d-54ce-b8ff-ae2b11780084" :step/math-academy-id 26332 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101782}}] :activity/title "Optimization Problems Involving Boxes and Trays" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186101068}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559908} :activity/id #uuid "d39c546e-aa9b-57f9-9da7-aa0899e1ca37" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050100 :topic/id #uuid "2d1d35b9-13b1-5815-b3ec-f38b609cdc4c" :topic/math-academy-id 1213} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559908 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559851 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fbea327-41aa-5fdc-a977-23866bec8887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$10$ units" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559179} {:answer/id #uuid "534e43c0-1360-5b0d-8a4a-5d2bde094e21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$5$ units" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559228} {:answer/id #uuid "f00913c9-54b0-51ef-a4b0-ef296a0170c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ units" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559598} {:answer/id #uuid "f0dc00a2-c124-5ff2-b78f-80d14094484c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$15$ units" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559603} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a02da5-372b-5869-879e-c7b98972e685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2$ units" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559617}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559228} :answer-field/id #uuid "907188cd-1b8a-5efd-a8a3-c00dedfb9afa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559725}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bae7b49c-3856-514a-a9ab-b99ea914cf24" :question/math-academy-id "q-117054" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2cfba1072b37cd316349997201ada6e67af702926214abec22a1ef5ae6543c5a.png)\n\nConsider a box with a square base with side lengths $x$ and height $y,$ as shown above. The volume of the box is $125$ cubic units. Given that the surface area of the box has been minimized, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: We need to find the value of $x$ such that the surface area\n\n$$\nS=2{x}^{2}+4xy\n$$\n\nis the smallest possible value.\n\n**Step 2**: The volume is exactly $125$ cubic units. So, we have the constraint equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =x\\cdot x\\cdot y \\\\ 125 & ={x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We make $y$ the subject of the constraint equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y & =125 \\\\ y & =\\frac{125}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute the above into our expression for $S,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2{x}^{2}+4xy \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+4x\\cdot \\frac{125}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+\\frac{500}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We solve the equation ${S}^{′}(x)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{S}^{′}(x)=4x-\\frac{500}{{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ 4x-\\frac{500}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{500}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ 4{x}^{3} & =500 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =125 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We confirm that $x=5$ is a minimum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{S}^{″}(x)=4+\\frac{1\\,000}{{x}^{3}}\\,⟹\\,{S}^{″}(5)=4+8=12>0.\n$$\n\nSince ${S}^{″}(5)$ is positive, we conclude that $x=5$ is indeed a minimum of $S(x).$\n\nTherefore, the box with the smallest possible surface area has side length $x=5$ units."} :step/id #uuid "2470c84c-c97b-513d-8e62-311c5ead05dc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559954}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559917 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559793 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd9f3f04-dec2-59a4-90c7-4e80640a9ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559638}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559638} :answer-field/id #uuid "41fc7962-a273-588e-89ef-1ba97b8bff24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "35d621eb-cf33-51a5-9f2c-6f01d51e0a4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-347273" :question/problem "![](images/12/12a9961800e0578de92b428e1a1a6ba5e10e25fe635a90f85c772f9bf73dc997.png)\n\nA piece of cardboard measures $15\\,cm\\times 7\\,cm.$ A tray of height $y\\,\\text{cm}$ is formed by cutting a $y\\times y\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}$ square from each of the corners and folding up the sides, as shown in the diagram. Determine the height $y$ of the box that gives the maximum possible volume.\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}} $\\text{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: We need to find the values of $x,y,$ and $z$ such that the volume\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nis the greatest possible value.\n\n**Step 2**: Notice that the width $x$ and the depth $z$ of the tray are given by\n\n$$\nx=15-2y,\\,z=7-2y.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $x>0$ and $z>0,$ we must have that $15-2y>0$ and $7-2y>0$, hence $y<\\frac{7}{2}.$ Therefore, the range of validity for $y$ is $0<y<\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\n**Step 3**: Substituting the above into the expression for $V,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =xyz \\\\  & =(15-2y)(y)(7-2y) \\\\  & =4{y}^{3}-44{y}^{2}+105y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We solve the equation ${V}^{′}(y)=0.$ Taking the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(y)=12{y}^{2}-88y+105,\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(y) & =0 \\\\ 12{y}^{2}-88y+105 & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\frac{35}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe discard $\\frac{35}{6}$ since we already know that $0<y<\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\n**Step 5**: We confirm that $\\frac{3}{2}$ is a maximum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{V}^{″}(y)=24y-88.\n$$\n\nSince ${V}^{″}(\\frac{3}{2})$ is negative, we conclude that $\\frac{3}{2}$ is indeed a maximum of $V(y).$\n\nTherefore, the height of the box with the maximum volume is $y=\\frac{3}{2}\\text{ cm}.$"} :step/id #uuid "3eaa5e01-60b9-5696-a1e7-991044c7bbba"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559946 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26d46271-3014-5476-b936-8ff5de06d051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559112}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559112} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ae05d3c-21d9-5363-8872-60ad0b3f9a59" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "88d64cef-5be0-59d0-8f76-951d4350e51b" :question/math-academy-id "q-347083" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d67ba70d92807f0a7298fb8222252a047f7eec03a26878a5aa95b0fb82a7335c.png)\n\nA box with no lid whose depth $z$ is $3$ times its height $y$ has a manufacturing cost that depends on two materials. The material for the base costs $$2$ per square meter, and the material for the lateral faces costs $$1$ per square meter. The box must have a volume of $972\\,{m}^{3}.$\n\nWhat is the value of $z$ for the box that has the smallest production cost? Do not round the answer.\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}} units" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: We need to find the value of $z$ such that the manufacturing cost\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2xz+1\\cdot 2xy+1\\cdot 2yz \\\\  & =2xz+2xy+2yz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis the smallest possible value.\n\n**Step 2**: The volume must be $972\\,{m}^{3}.$ So, we have the constraint equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =x\\cdot z\\cdot y \\\\ 972 & =x\\cdot z\\cdot (\\frac{z}{3}) \\\\ 972 & =\\frac{1}{3}x{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We make $x$ the subject of the constraint equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}x{z}^{2} & =972 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2916}{{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute the above into our expression for $C,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2xz+2xy+2yz \\\\  & =2\\,(\\frac{2916}{{z}^{2}})\\,z+2\\,(\\frac{2916}{{z}^{2}})\\,(\\frac{z}{3})+2\\,(\\frac{z}{3})\\,z \\\\  & =\\frac{5832}{z}+\\frac{1944}{z}+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7776}{z}+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We solve the equation ${C}^{′}(z)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{C}^{′}(z)=\\frac{4}{3}z-\\frac{7776}{{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}z-\\frac{7776}{{z}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{z}^{3} & =7776 \\\\ {z}^{3} & =5832 \\\\ z & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We confirm that $z=18$ is a minimum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{C}^{″}(z)=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{15552}{{z}^{3}}\\,⟹\\,{C}^{″}(18)=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{8}{3}=4>0.\n$$\n\nSince ${C}^{″}(18)$ is positive, we conclude that $z=18$ is indeed a minimum of $C(z).$\n\nTherefore, the production cost is the smallest when $z=18$ units."} :step/id #uuid "83c4667d-a7a5-57bc-aaae-222f06c3f1de" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559917}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559954 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02932fbd-ee3d-58bf-9d40-e6c4b5772ce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559022} {:answer/id #uuid "0653430e-b3f6-5da7-8b4a-42f0139025c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559029} {:answer/id #uuid "13d2aacc-5287-5151-8fa4-4b990a54d3bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{7}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559061} {:answer/id #uuid "2c37baac-a6d7-52ff-b039-36b9f3d4538b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{5}{3}}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559127} {:answer/id #uuid "72638d95-8910-5c23-aa5c-c06b64acc003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559302}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559302} :answer-field/id #uuid "76985055-fc94-55ff-998a-6e253b938977" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8973c685-fd2c-51e0-89ff-171e4339d4cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-117217" :question/problem "![](images/af/afc68dbb5c336cff31e75f5ed92dd853c8fc7ec43e8fa66539d27d83b9e2070f.png)\n\nA box with no lid and a square base has a manufacturing cost that depends on two materials. The material for the base costs $$3$ per square meter, and the material for the lateral faces costs $$5$ per square meter. The box must have a volume of $2\\,{m}^{3}.$\n\nWhat is the value of $x$ for the box that has the smallest production cost?" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: We need to find the value of $x$ such that the manufacturing cost\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =3{x}^{2}+5\\cdot 4xy \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+20xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis the smallest possible value.\n\n**Step 2**: The volume must be $2\\,{m}^{3}.$ So, we have the constraint equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =x\\cdot x\\cdot y \\\\ 2 & ={x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We make $y$ the subject of the constraint equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y & =2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute the above into our expression for $C,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =3{x}^{2}+20xy \\\\ C & =3{x}^{2}+20x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ C & =3{x}^{2}+\\frac{40}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We solve the equation ${C}^{′}(x)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{C}^{′}(x)=6x-\\frac{40}{{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ 6x-\\frac{40}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 6{x}^{3} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =\\frac{20}{3} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We confirm that $x=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}}$ is a minimum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{C}^{″}(x)=6+\\frac{80}{{x}^{3}}\\,⟹\\,{C}^{″}(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}})=6+12=18>0.\n$$\n\nSince ${C}^{″}(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}})$ is positive, we conclude that $x=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}}$ is indeed a minimum of $C(x).$"} :step/id #uuid "986d328c-4039-5272-94a8-a5b54b4004c1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559960}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559960 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559798 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3088ae4-d68a-57e8-b0d8-0c5b606e66de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "648" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559463}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559463} :answer-field/id #uuid "29d8dbeb-a278-5ecd-a7ab-cdc1d19cdc10" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3b6389e0-fab8-5e1d-bb5a-1e8d075edcaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-346784" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4cafc2891cfd957aad10e876d51757e8c6d7e84844927cb57ce1c2e704fe5b55.png)\n\nConsider a box with width $x,$ height $y,$ and depth $z,$ as shown above. The depth of the box is three times its width. Given that the box's volume is $972$ cubic units, what is the smallest possible surface area ${S}_{\\text{min}}$ of the box? Do not round the answer.\n\n${S}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}} square units" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: We need to find the value of $x$ such that the surface area\n\n$$\nS=2xz+2xy+2yz\n$$\n\nis the smallest possible value.\n\n**Step 2**: The volume is $972$ cubic units. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =x\\cdot y\\cdot z \\\\ 972 & =xyz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that $z=3x,$ we get the constraint equation\n\n$$\n972=3{x}^{2}y.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We make $y$ the subject of the constraint equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}y & =972 \\\\ y & =\\frac{324}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute the above into our expression for $S,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2xz+2xy+2yz \\\\  & =2x(3x)+2x(\\frac{324}{{x}^{2}})+2(\\frac{324}{{x}^{2}})(3x) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+\\frac{648}{x}+\\frac{1944}{x} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+\\frac{2592}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We solve the equation ${S}^{′}(x)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{S}^{′}(x)=12x-\\frac{2592}{{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ 12x-\\frac{2592}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 12{x}^{3}-2592 & =0 \\\\ 12{x}^{3} & =2592 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =216 \\\\ x & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We confirm that $x=6$ is a minimum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{S}^{″}(x)=12+\\frac{5184}{{x}^{3}}\\,⟹\\,{S}^{″}(6)=12+24=36>0.\n$$\n\nSince ${S}^{″}(6)$ is positive, we conclude that $x=6$ is indeed a minimum.\n\nNow, the smallest surface area ${S}_{\\text{min}}$ that the box can have is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\text{min}}=S(6) & =6(6)^{2}+\\frac{2592}{6} \\\\  & =648\\,\\text{square units}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "afee5c19-21de-5dac-b2a9-ef66458e0dec" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559946}}] :activity/title "Optimization Problems Involving Boxes and Trays" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559011}]}
